title: "Exact Primal-Dual Certificates for a Two-Bidder, Two-Item Auction"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Fang
    given-names: Jiarui
    affiliation: Boston University
    email: baymin@bu.edu
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-9100-0445"
version: 1.4.0
date-released: 2026-09-06
repository-code: "https://github.com/Baymax-ray/two-bidder-two-item-dsic-certificates"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Complete functional exchanges and a common capacity-price certificate
  give a rigorous interval for the two-bidder, two-item independent-uniform
  randomized pointwise-DSIC auction. The explicit mechanism has exact
  algebraic revenue 0.8764641644717980499449... and the unrestricted upper
  is 0.8829230532587169692606..., giving a gap below 0.006459 and more
  than 99.2684% of optimal revenue. Occupied-region utility identities
  solve full randomized conditional screening on specified actual residuals.
  A reusable support and sparse long-range IC cycles solve both charged
  screening values under a common measure. Independent full-revenue
  integration and continuous upper replays support the endpoints.
  The unrestricted optimum and a matching auction remain open.
